//? Title: DeepLab v3 global context and separable v3+ decoding
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Pixel classification needs both wide scene context and local boundary detail. DeepLab v3 adds image-level context to atrous features;v3+ combines separable context branches with low-level decoding. This report checks complete tensor graphs before fitting both compact models with explicit Adam.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.7_segmentation/deeplab_v3_plus.cpp`.

> The method

Five ASPP branches concatenate local,multiscale and global features. The optional separable decoder combines this context with a projected C2 map at stride4. Global means,dilated kernels,BN state and all fitting/evaluation arithmetic use tensors.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/deeplab_v3_plus_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/deeplab_v3_plus_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/deeplab_v3_plus_concept.tikz > build/deeplab_v3_plus_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/deeplab_v3_plus_concept.svg build/deeplab_v3_plus_concept.dvi > build/deeplab_v3_plus_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
