> A global image branch with exact input derivatives

DeepLab v3's context module concatenates five branches:1x1 projection,three
atrous3x3 convolutions and a global image-average projection. The image branch
computes a spatial mean,normalizes/projects it,and broadcasts back by aligned-
corner bilinear resizing. A constant projected mean is therefore constant
across spatial locations;it still receives gradients from every output pixel.

This fixture fixes an identity1x1 projection and compensates the stored BN
variance offset,so each positive input channel's global mean broadcasts exactly.
The derivative of the sum of every repeated output is1 for every source pixel.
Native independent calculations check separate batches/channels and all pixels.
Training at N=1 makes the1x1 global BN batch variance zero;the compact fit uses
batch4 and the warmed moving-state path uses inference mode.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/deeplab_v3_plus_global.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::ParameterStore p(17), state(18);
  m::ConvNormConfig cfg;
  cfg.scale = true;
  cfg.epsilon = 1e-5;
  auto x = (.7 + .4 * n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 2 * 7 * 9 * 2)))
               .reshape({2, 7, 9, 2})
               .requires_grad_();
  {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    m::ImagePoolBranch(p, state, "pool", x, 2, cfg);
  }
  p.set("pool/project/W", n::eye(2).reshape({1, 1, 2, 2}));
  p.set("pool/project/bn/gamma", n::full({2}, std::sqrt(1. + cfg.epsilon)));
  const auto out = m::ImagePoolBranch(p, state, "pool", x, 2, cfg),
             g = n::grad(n::sum(out), {x})[0], means = n::mean(x, {1, 2}, true);
  if (n::max(n::abs(g - 1.)).item() > 1e-5 || n::max(n::abs(out - means)).item() > 1e-5)
    return 1;
  const auto input =
                 n::slice_axis(n::slice_axis(x.detach(), 0, 0, 1), 3, 0, 1).reshape({7, 9}),
             context = n::slice_axis(n::slice_axis(out, 0, 0, 1), 3, 0, 1).reshape({7, 9});
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(input, .3, 1.2), b = n::plot_tensor_map(context, .3, 1.2);
  a.title("Known spatial input channel");
  b.title("Projected global mean broadcast");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(a).add(b).size(1200, 550).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/deeplab_v3_plus_global.svg");
  std::print("Separate per-image/channel means broadcast;all252 source derivatives are1 "
             "within1e-5. First channel mean {:.6f}. Fixed BN compensation isolates the "
             "operation without fitting.\n",
             means.at({0, 0, 0, 0}));
}
```
