> Full v3/v3+ graphs and the separable decoder

Both models use a supported output-stride16 ResNet50 encoder. V3 concatenates
ordinary ASPP features,projects1x1 and classifies. V3+ uses atrous depthwise/
pointwise blocks in ASPP,projects C2 to48 channels,fuses at stride4 and applies
two separable decoder blocks before linear class scores. Each depthwise stage
has BN/ReLU before its pointwise normalized projection. This is the source's
ResNet-based variant;it does not claim the paper's Xception backbone.

Full v3/v3+ learned counts are39,048,533/26,696,133,state56,192/70,720 and
179/203 learned tensor gradients. Both full backwards execute below at33px.
Compact ResNet18/divisor8 uses head32,rates1/2/3,decoder32/low8,no dropout:
241,740/198,004 learned and1,584/2,256 state scalars. Native checks require
all compact gradients nonzero and verify five branches concatenate160 channels.
Stride8 doubles base atrous rates and preserves learned parameter shapes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  for (bool plus : {false, true}) {
    n::ParameterStore p(17), state(18);
    m::DeepLabV3Config c;
    c.decoder = plus;
    const auto net = m::DeepLabV3(
        p, state, n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 33 * 33 * 3)).reshape({1, 33, 33, 3}), c, true);
    const auto g = n::grad(n::mean(n::square(net.logits)), p.parameters());
    if (p.count() != (plus ? 26696133 : 39048533) || state.count() != (plus ? 70720 : 56192) ||
        g.size() != (plus ? 203 : 179) || net.branches.size() != 5)
      return 1;
    for (const auto &v : g)
      if (!v.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(v.to(n::DType::Float64))).item()))
        return 1;
    std::print("Full{}:{} learned/{} state scalars,all{} finite defined gradients at33px,five "
               "ASPP branches.\n",
               plus ? "v3+" : "v3", p.count(), state.count(), g.size());
  }
}
```
