> Native confusion matrices

These matrices use the held-out predictions from the executed program above.
The native `ConfusionMatrix` SVG API labels exact counts with true classes
running from top to bottom and predicted classes from left to right.

\image(figures/deeplab_v3_plus_confusion_api_0.svg)
\caption(Held-out pixel/voxel confusion counts, evaluation 1. Exact cell counts are printed in the image.)
\alttext(Integer prediction counts with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)

\image(figures/deeplab_v3_plus_confusion_api_0_normalized.svg)
\caption(True-class normalized confusion: each nonempty row sums to 100%; zero-support rows remain zero.)
\alttext(Row-normalized percentages with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)

